{#-
  about.html.j2: /about/ (Milestone 2 step 7). The text is site/content/about.md, rendered
  by tff_site.pages (raw HTML off). Context: every page's, plus `heading` and `content`. No
  script: the page needs none. Styles: site/css/40-pages.css.

  The page closes with the note "Why isn't my favorite free font here?" (site ruling of
  2026-09-29, why_not_listed), which moved here from the front page on 2026-10-07
  (why_not_listed_to_about). Its words are the owner's Draft A of 2026-11-21, four paragraphs
  word for word (why_not_listed_conversation, data/reviews/site/2026-11-21.toml). It lives in
  this template rather than about.md for its stable anchor, #why-not-listed, which the front
  page's empty-search message links to, and for its links: "The four rules above" goes to the
  rules, #which-fonts-are-listed, the id tff_site.pages gives about.md's "## Which fonts are
  listed"; the address is a mailto link to site.feedback.email; and the last paragraph is the
  tip pitch (funding_pitch, 2026-09-30; tip_jar, 2026-10-05), whose "leave a tip" is one plain
  link to site.tip_url, like the nav's Tip Jar. That paragraph shows only when site.tip_url is
  set, as the nav's link does.
-#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block scripts %}{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
<article class="page page-prose">
<h1>{{ heading }}</h1>
{{ content }}
<h2 id="why-not-listed">Why isn't my favorite free font here?</h2>
<p>Usually it's the license. Free to download isn't always free to use. Some fonts are free only for personal projects or as a trial, or only if you never change or embed them. Others come with terms that can reach into the documents or products you make with them.</p>
<p>We list only fonts whose licenses let anyone use them in any project, personal or commercial, with no use restrictions. We read each font's own license text rather than trusting a label. <a href="#which-fonts-are-listed">The four rules above</a> give the details.</p>
<p>Sometimes the license is fine, but the font is used less than the ones ranked here. Those fonts will be listed later, A–Z. If you think one belongs here now, email <a href="mailto:{{ site.feedback.email }}">{{ site.feedback.email }}</a> and ask us to consider it.</p>
{% if site.tip_url %}
<p>Checking every license takes time. If the list has helped you, please <a href="{{ site.tip_url }}">leave a tip</a>.</p>
{% endif %}
</article>
{% endblock %}
